1. NVIDIA TAO PyTorch backend
-----------------------------
    Source   : https://github.com/NVIDIA/tao_pytorch_backend
    Version  : Release/7.0.1 (d99ff772e2cff894015d81a96d2cb92119000e19)
    License  : Apache License 2.0
    Copyright: (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES

    NOT redistributed. `scripts/setup_tao_backend.sh` clones it from upstream at
    the pinned commit.

    We modify five files. Rather than vendor a fork, we ship only the diff, at
    `patches/tao_sparse4d_gaugealign.patch`, so it stays unambiguous which lines
    are NVIDIA's and which are ours:

      nvidia_tao_pytorch/cv/backbone_v2/__init__.py
          lazy backbone imports, so absent optional dependencies do not break a
          ResNet-50 model
      nvidia_tao_pytorch/cv/sparse4d/model/sparse4d_head.py
          pass max_time_interval through to the instance bank (1 line)
      nvidia_tao_pytorch/cv/sparse4d/model/ops/setup_ext.py       (new file)
          build script for the deformable-aggregation CUDA extension
      nvidia_tao_pytorch/cv/sparse4d/model/instance_bank.py
          our CVC-Assoc learned survival gate and cross-view consensus hooks;
          both disabled by default
      nvidia_tao_pytorch/cv/sparse4d/model/criterion.py
          optional background-query loss term, used only in the fine-tuning
          study; disabled by default

    Modifications are (c) 2026 the GaugeAlign authors and are licensed under
    Apache License 2.0, matching the files they modify, as required by that
    license. Modified files carry NVIDIA's original copyright notices.


